    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-membership",
      "narrative": "Harris assigns the dominant 7th chord to the major 6 diminished scale family. Every dom7 chord belongs to a family of four related dominants sharing the same diminished triad, built a major 3rd above the dominant note. 'The rule of thumb for finding a related diminished chord is to build it a major 3rd above the dominant note.' Chapter 1, p. 27.",
