      "granularity_name": "voice-leading"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-reclassification",
      "narrative": "Harris collapses the min7 chord into the major 6 diminished scale family by redefining it as an inversion: 'Every minor 7 chord is an inversion of a major 6th chord.' The student should think of any m7 chord not as its own category but as a major 6th chord viewed from a different inversion, unlocking all major-6-diminished voicings for min7 contexts. Chapter 3, p. 69.",
