    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "voicing-source-scale",
      "narrative": "Because every min7 chord is an inversion of a major 6th chord, all voicings for a min7 chord are drawn from the major 6 diminished scale of the corresponding major 6th chord. The student assigns the min7 to that scale and applies the standard movable-chord voice-leading rules. Chapter 3, p. 69-71.",
