      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "important-minor-function",
      "narrative": "Harris names a special role for the min7 chord: 'Important minor is the term given to the chord found on the 5th degree of a dominant 7th scale (5 of 5).' This specific min7\u2014the minor 7th a 5th above the dominant\u2014serves as a reusable harmonic tool in progressions like Rhythm Changes. Chapter 2, p. 46.",
