    {
      "chord_quality": "min7b5",
      "function_role": "harmonic-family-reclassification",
      "narrative": "Harris collapses the min7b5 (half-diminished) chord into the minor 6 diminished scale family: 'every minor7 flat5 chord is an inversion of a minor 6th chord.' The student should think of any m7b5 as a minor 6th chord in inversion, unlocking all minor-6-diminished voicings for half-diminished contexts. Chapter 3, p. 69.",
