      "narrative": "Because every m7b5 chord is an inversion of a minor 6th chord, all voicings are drawn from the minor 6 diminished scale of the corresponding minor 6th chord. The movable-chord rule applies: move each note to the next note of the minor 6 diminished scale. Chapter 3, p. 69-71.",
