      "function_role": "minor-6-diminished-scale-construction",
      "narrative": "The minor 6 diminished scale is constructed by fusing the minor 6 chord with its related diminished chord: 'This scale is formed by combining a minor 6 chord with its related diminished chord. The diminished chord is built from a major 3rd above the dominant note of the scale.' Chapter 2, p. 58.",
