      "chord_quality": "min6",
      "function_role": "major-minor-minor6-voice-leading",
      "narrative": "Harris prescribes a specific named voice-leading unit ending on a minor-with-6th-in-bass chord: 'the progression from major to minor to minor with the 6th degree in the bass: (Bb major-G minor-Gm/E).' The min6 position is the cadential arrival of this three-chord formula. Chapter 4, p. 79.",
