    {
      "chord_quality": "dim7",
      "function_role": "related-diminished-chord-locator",
      "narrative": "Harris prescribes building the related diminished chord a major 3rd above the dominant note to locate the four interchangeable dominant 7th chords in any key. 'Just go up a major 3rd from the root of the dominant 7th chord.' Chapter 1, p. 27; Chapter 2, p. 42.",
